llvm-3.7.1 local rule: at -O2 the unit pipeline's LoopUnswitch unswitches a
loop non-trivially on a branch whose whole condition is loop-invariant
(no upstream state)

This patch CHANGES THE UNIT PIPELINE ONLY (PassManagerBuilder::
populateModulePassManager). Two changes, nothing else:
  PassManagerBuilder.cpp:247: the pass is built with OptimizeForSize only
    under a size level or below -O2 (3.7.1: below -O3), so at -O2 it may
    unswitch non-trivially, as -O3 builds it; nothing else of -O3 (not the
    275 inliner, not ArgumentPromotion);
  LoopUnswitch.cpp, UnswitchIfProfitable, before the size refusal: a
    non-trivial unswitch is refused unless the candidate is a conditional
    branch and the invariant found is its whole condition. A switch, a select
    and an invariant part of an and/or keep the refusal the size flag gave
    them.
Unchanged: trivial unswitches (done at every level, as before); the cost
test (CostAllowsUnswitching, -loop-unswitch-threshold 100); the link stage,
which has no LoopUnswitch (addLTOOptimizationPasses); the second instance
under -extra-vectorizer-passes (off). The library line (3.3) is another
compiler. At -O3 the refusal of switches, selects and parts applies too
(nothing in the tree is built at -O3 with this compiler).

Question (rounds 514E, 544D, 547D): the base splits loops on a count being
0 (group R: FUN_013e5560 and five copies, `frames.resize(n)` over each key's
frame set: the shift hoisted by LICM above the test, the zero copy
specialised by GVN after the clone). 3.7.1's -O2 builds the pass with
OptimizeForSize, which refuses every non-trivial unswitch (LoopUnswitch.cpp
:691, after the cost test at :681); the game's unit pipeline today performs
no unswitch of any kind (round 544D, variant notriv: 0 of 6,568 units
change with trivial unswitching off as well).

Evidence (scratch d544/, d547/). Stage 1 of every unit run by the line's own
opt with clang's exact -O2 pass list and a loadable copy of this
LoopUnswitch.cpp; controls equal to the tree's build in every unit (6,568
and 6,569 bitcode files byte-identical, 0 functions differ).
  The stock -O3 argument alone: 5 rows lost (0x968550, 0x9685a0, 0x9685f0: a
    select on a bool argument, `if (enable) f |= 4; else f &= ~4` in a loop,
    the base keeps `test sil, sil; cmove` inside it; 0xed1fc0: a switch,
    sndx; 0xefae90: the invariant part of `ids && i < idCount`, sndx).
  No loop-size threshold separates them (the lost loops measure 9 to 12,
    the won 17 to 58).
  This rule (branch on a whole invariant condition, every prefix): 0 rows
    lost; 12 functions equal, group R x6 (0x13e5560, 0x13fae50, 0x141ce50,
    0x143d9c0, 0x1449480, 0x14677a0: 288 to 425 bytes, the base's), the
    slot 3 resizes x3 (0x13f0770, 0x13f5e70, 0x14873b0, 441 bytes) and the
    same with a third value x3 (0x13f0fa0, 0x13f66a0, 0x1487be0, 457);
    3 toward the base (0x113f570 0.35 to 0.97, 0xa70ec0 0.11 to 0.31,
    0xabbfd0 to the base's structure).
  Sites against: none among the 14 base functions with two loop copies
    whose drafts the rule does not give (d547 step4_fourteen.txt: each a
    developer's two loops over different data).

Source forms the bytes exclude: the loop unswitched by hand (group R: 440
bytes against the base's 425, round 514E); the plain loop under the stock
pass (288 and 304 bytes against 425, 441 and 457).

NO upstream state. Every release from 3.3 to 4.0.0 takes branches,
switches, selects and and/or parts alike and builds the -O2 pass with
OptimizeForSize (d547 step1_public_form.txt). Sony authorship of this is not
shown.

Refuted by: ONE matched row whose base bytes keep a branch on a whole
loop-invariant condition inside a loop that the cost test would allow (a
loop of at most 100 instructions, not a copy of an unswitched one).

diff -ru a/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp b/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp
--- a/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp
@@ -244,7 +244,10 @@
   // Rotate Loop - disable header duplication at -Oz
   MPM.add(createLoopRotatePass(SizeLevel == 2 ? 0 : -1));
   MPM.add(createLICMPass());                  // Hoist loop invariants
-  MPM.add(createLoopUnswitchPass(SizeLevel || OptLevel < 3));
+  // Local rule (unswitch-01): from -O2 the pass is built without
+  // OptimizeForSize; it refuses every non-trivial condition but a branch's
+  // whole one (LoopUnswitch.cpp, UnswitchIfProfitable).
+  MPM.add(createLoopUnswitchPass(SizeLevel || OptLevel < 2));
   MPM.add(createInstructionCombiningPass());
   MPM.add(createIndVarSimplifyPass());        // Canonicalize indvars
   MPM.add(createLoopIdiomPass());             // Recognize idioms like memset.
diff -ru a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/LoopUnswitch.cpp b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/LoopUnswitch.cpp
--- a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/LoopUnswitch.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/LoopUnswitch.cpp
@@ -687,6 +687,12 @@
     return false;
   }
 
+  // Local rule (unswitch-01): a non-trivial unswitch only on a conditional
+  // branch whose whole condition is loop-invariant. A switch, a select (both
+  // come without TI) and an invariant part of an and/or are refused.
+  if (!TI || LoopCond != cast<BranchInst>(TI)->getCondition())
+    return false;
+
   // Do not do non-trivial unswitch while optimizing for size.
   if (OptimizeForSize || F->hasFnAttribute(Attribute::OptimizeForSize))
     return false;
